{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node1 has at least 512 MB of compressed in-memory swap preferred over disk-backed swap.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observations before and after reboot show /dev/zram0 configured as 512 MiB zstd-compressed swap at priority 100, while /dev/vda2 disk swap has priority -2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-adadbd2f89cc4395","cmd-094e96cddf5d4219"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The compressed in-memory swap activates automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The zram service was enabled and active before restart. After an acknowledged reboot with a changed boot identity, the system returned to running state with the service enabled and active and /dev/zram0 restored as swap.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b866de2c252544fe","cmd-adadbd2f89cc4395","cmd-9ed6d061814c4988","cmd-cce3aeeaf6e04a22","cmd-094e96cddf5d4219","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Loading and probing zram established the required capability; writing and correcting the unit produced the final configuration; enabling it activated the requested service; and the reboot was required both to verify boot persistence and to fulfill the restart protocol. No failed services, package damage, new exposure, or executor-created temporary residue was observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff3defac609645dd","cmd-e018457286f84878","cmd-b866de2c252544fe","cmd-9ed6d061814c4988","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. node1 has persistent 512 MiB zstd zram swap at priority 100, preferred over the existing priority -2 disk swap. The mandatory restart protocol is coherently evidenced by the pre-restart healthy task state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered running system and swap service.","limitations":[]}
